WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.630
Here is how to fill your financial
cockpit.

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.430
Follow this example, then use your own
numbers.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.710
Estimates are fine. Tap Start.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.580
Step one, enter monthly take home income
after

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.500
taxes. Our example uses $6,000. If you

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.320
enter one paycheck instead, choose how
often you

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:20.820
get paid.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.740
Step two, add your monthly must pays,
housing,

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:30.980
utilities, groceries, insurance, and
minimum debt payments. We

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.220
enter $3,400.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.260
Step three, enter a typical month of
wants,

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.900
like dining out, subscriptions, and
shopping. Our example

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:42.900
uses $1,200.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.720
Step four, enter what you save each month.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.900
We use $500. If you save zero, tap

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:52.520
none right now.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:58.390
Step five, enter only debt payments above
the

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.970
minimums. Minimum payments are already in
needs. Our

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:04.390
example pays $250 extra.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:10.110
Step six, add the debt balances you owe

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:13.750
today. Include car loans, credit cards,
student loans,

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:16.670
personal loans, and medical bills. Leave
out your

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:17.090
mortgage.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.990
Step seven, enter emergency savings, then
your goal.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:26.610
We have $4,000 saved and an $8

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:30.810
,000 goal. Use three months suggests
$10,200

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.830
based on this example's needs.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.780
Step eight, enter the current value of
money

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.780
already invested. Retirement accounts
count. We enter $2

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.680
,500, tap none yet if you have not

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:45.080
started.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.380
Step nine, choose what feels most
pressing. We

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:54.140
select stable. Pick a short term objective
if

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.760
you want. We choose build a cushion, then

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.100
tap run my flight check.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.340
This example produces 71 cruise control.
Read your

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.560
report and choose your next seven day
move.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.500
Your result will reflect your own answers.
Education only.
